# Patient Journey AI Chatbot — Implementation Plan

## Overview

A doctor-facing AI chat interface that allows querying, analyzing, and updating 1,000 patient records stored in Supabase. A doctor can type a Patient ID (or partial name), the system fetches the full record, feeds it as context into a chat session with an LLM (e.g. Google Gemini or OpenAI), and the doctor can then ask follow-up questions or issue natural-language commands to update the record. The entire conversation keeps context across turns.

---

## CSV Data Structure (Existing)

The CSV has **1,001 records** with the following columns:

| Column | Type | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `Patient ID` | UUID | `921d93d1-17b8-426f-abae-5b16c7e5cd93` |
| `Name` | Text | `Debra Griffith` |
| `Date of Birth` | Date | `1971-04-01` |
| `Gender` | Text | `Female` |
| `Medical Condition` | Text | `Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease` |
| `Treatments` | Text | `Medication` |
| `Doctor's Notes` | Text | `Patient requires home oxygen therapy.` |
| `Admit Date` | Date | `2021-07-12` |
| `Discharge Date` | Date | `2021-07-13` |
| `Bill Amount` | Decimal | `14651.34` |

> [!NOTE]
> We'll add extra mutable fields to the Supabase table: `current_status`, `additional_conditions` (array), `updated_at`, and `updated_by` to support doctor-driven updates.

