## Proposed Changes

### 1. Supabase Setup

#### [NEW] `supabase/schema.sql`
Create the patient records table with extended mutable fields:

```sql
create table patients (
  id uuid primary key,                        -- from CSV "Patient ID"
  name text not null,
  date_of_birth date,
  gender text,
  medical_condition text,
  treatments text,
  doctors_notes text,
  admit_date date,
  discharge_date date,
  bill_amount numeric(10,2),
  -- Extended fields for doctor updates
  current_status text,
  additional_conditions text[],               -- array of new conditions added
  additional_notes text,                      -- doctor's live updates
  updated_at timestamptz default now(),
  updated_by uuid references auth.users(id)
);

-- Row Level Security: only authenticated doctors can read/write
alter table patients enable row level security;
create policy "Authenticated users can read patients"
  on patients for select using (auth.role() = 'authenticated');
create policy "Authenticated users can update patients"
  on patients for update using (auth.role() = 'authenticated');
```

#### [NEW] `supabase/seed_patients.mjs`
A one-time Node.js script to parse the CSV and bulk-insert 1,000 records into Supabase using the service role key.

