### 3. Core Feature Flows

#### A. Patient Lookup
```
Doctor types Patient ID or name
    → /api/patient/search?q=921d93d1  (or ?q=Debra)
    → Supabase query: SELECT * WHERE id = ? OR name ILIKE ?
    → Return full patient record
    → Display PatientCard in sidebar
    → Auto-inject record as first AI context message
```

#### B. AI Chat with Patient Context
```
Doctor asks: "What medication should I adjust for this patient?"
    → POST /api/chat
    → Body: { messages: [...history], patientId, patientRecord }
    → Server builds system prompt:
        "You are a medical AI assistant. Here is the full patient record:
         Name: Debra Griffith | Condition: COPD | Treatment: Medication |
         Notes: Patient requires home oxygen therapy..."
    → Send to Gemini API with full conversation history
    → Stream response back to frontend
    → Append to chat window
```

#### C. Natural-Language Record Update
```
Doctor: "Add hypertension to this patient's conditions"
    → AI detects update intent (via function calling or keyword detection)
    → AI responds: "I'll add Hypertension to the additional conditions.
                    Shall I confirm this update?"
    → UpdateConfirmModal appears with diff preview
    → Doctor clicks Confirm
    → PATCH /api/patient/[id]
        Body: { additional_conditions: [...existing, "Hypertension"] }
    → Supabase updates record
    → PatientCard refreshes in sidebar
    → AI acknowledges: "Updated. Hypertension has been added."
```

#### D. Conversation Context Persistence
- All messages stored in React state (`useState`) for the session
- Full history sent with every API call so Gemini has full context
- Optionally: save to Supabase `conversations` table for persistence across sessions

